#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:1
msgid "Cluster TMA: Multicast and SM-to-SM Copy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:3
msgid ""
"This page describes two advanced data-movement features that are available "
"on NVIDIA Hopper (SM90) and later: **TMA multicast** and **SM-to-SM cluster "
"copy**. Both features are exposed through extensions to the existing `T."
"copy` operator and require a kernel launched with `T.ClusterKernel`, i.e., "
"with `cluster_dims != (1, 1, 1)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:8
msgid "Requirements:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:9
msgid "CUDA Compute Capability ≥ 9.0 (Hopper / Blackwell / RTX 5090)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:13
msgid "Background: Thread Block Clusters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:15
msgid ""
"A *thread block cluster* is a group of CTAs that share a common virtual "
"address space for their shared-memory regions and can communicate without "
"going through global memory. Within a cluster, each CTA has a *block rank* "
"(0-indexed position inside the cluster), and all CTAs can observe each "
"other's shared memory via the `shared::cluster` address space."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:21
msgid ""
"with T.ClusterKernel(grid_x, grid_y, threads=128, cluster_dims=(4, 1, 1)) as "
"(bx, by):\n"
"    rank  = T.block_rank_in_cluster()   # 0..3 within this cluster\n"
"    T.cluster_sync()                     # barrier across all CTAs in "
"cluster\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:29
msgid "Feature 1 — TMA Multicast (`cluster_mask`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:31
#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:114
msgid "What it does"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:33
msgid ""
"Normally each CTA issues its own TMA load, fetching a tile from global "
"memory into its private shared memory. With multicast, **a single TMA "
"transaction broadcasts one global tile to every participating CTA "
"simultaneously**, saving repeated DRAM traffic when multiple CTAs in a "
"cluster need the same data (e.g., the same K-panel in a split-K GEMM)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:39
msgid ""
"Global memory ──TMA multicast──▶ shared memory (rank 0)\n"
"                              └─▶ shared memory (rank 1)   (same tile, no "
"extra DRAM read)\n"
"                  TMA load    ──▶ shared memory (rank 2)   (independent "
"tile)\n"
"                  TMA load    ──▶ shared memory (rank 3)   (independent "
"tile)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:46
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:48
msgid "T.copy_cluster(src_global, dst_shared, cluster_mask=<int>)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:52
msgid ""
"`cluster_mask` is a bitmask where each set bit identifies a CTA rank that "
"participates in the multicast. The CTA whose rank equals the lowest set bit "
"in the mask issues `cp.async.bulk.tensor … multicast::cluster`; every other "
"CTA in the mask receives the data passively (no instruction issued). CTAs "
"outside the mask perform a regular TMA load for their own tile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:58
msgid "Example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:60
msgid ""
"import tilelang\n"
"import tilelang.language as T\n"
"\n"
"def make_tma_multicast_kernel(M, N, block_M, block_N, cluster_mask):\n"
"    @T.prim_func\n"
"    def kernel(\n"
"        A: T.Tensor((M, N), \"float16\"),\n"
"        B: T.Tensor((M, N), \"float16\"),\n"
"    ):\n"
"        # 4 CTAs per cluster; ranks 0 and 1 share the same tile via "
"multicast.\n"
"        with T.ClusterKernel(\n"
"            T.ceildiv(N, block_N),\n"
"            T.ceildiv(M, block_M),\n"
"            threads=128,\n"
"            cluster_dims=(4, 1, 1)\n"
"        ) as (bx, by):\n"
"            A_shared = T.alloc_shared((block_M, block_N), \"float16\")\n"
"\n"
"            # cluster_mask=0b0011: ranks 0 and 1 participate.\n"
"            # Rank 0 issues tma_load_multicast; rank 1 receives passively.\n"
"            # Ranks 2 and 3 each issue a regular tma_load.\n"
"            T.copy_cluster(A[by * block_M, bx * block_N], A_shared,\n"
"                           cluster_mask=cluster_mask)\n"
"\n"
"            T.copy(A_shared, B[by * block_M, bx * block_N])\n"
"\n"
"    return kernel\n"
msgstr ""

