#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:135
msgid ""
"A copy region is *contiguous* when its innermost dimension spans the full "
"buffer width (i.e. the copy region `[..., 0:N_tile]` satisfies `N_tile == "
"buffer_shape[-1]`). If the innermost extent is shorter, the region is non-"
"contiguous and the TMA fast path is unavailable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:140
msgid "TMA fast path — bulk async copy with mbarrier"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:142
msgid ""
"T.copy_cluster(src_shared, dst_shared, dst_block=<rank>, "
"remote_barrier=<mbarrier>)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:146
msgid ""
"A single elected thread issues one `cp.async.bulk.shared::cluster` "
"instruction. The hardware DMA engine transfers the entire tile "
"asynchronously and signals the destination CTA's mbarrier on completion. The "
"destination CTA waits with `T.mbarrier_wait_parity`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:151
msgid "Steps:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:152
msgid ""
"Both CTAs allocate the **same** shared memory layout so their mbarriers live "
"at the same offset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:154
msgid ""
"Every CTA initialises its own barrier for 1 arrival via `T."
"alloc_cluster_barrier([1])`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:155
msgid ""
"The source CTA (`pid == 0` below) calls `T.copy_cluster(... dst_block=1, "
"remote_barrier=...)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:156
msgid "The destination CTA (`pid == 1`) waits on its local barrier copy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:158
msgid ""
"import tilelang\n"
"import tilelang.language as T\n"
"\n"
"@tilelang.jit(execution_backend=\"cython\")\n"
"def make_cluster_copy_kernel(N: int):\n"
"    @T.prim_func\n"
"    def kernel(\n"
"        A: T.Tensor((N,), \"float32\"),\n"
"        B: T.Tensor((N,), \"float32\"),\n"
"    ):\n"
"        with T.ClusterKernel(2, threads=128, cluster_dims=(2, 1, 1)) as "
"pid:\n"
"            s_src     = T.alloc_shared((N,), \"float32\")\n"
"            s_dst     = T.alloc_shared((N,), \"float32\")\n"
"            s_barrier = T.alloc_cluster_barrier([1])\n"
"\n"
"            T.fill(s_src, 0.0)\n"
"            T.fill(s_dst, 0.0)\n"
"\n"
"            T.cluster_sync()\n"
"\n"
"            if pid == 0:\n"
"                # Load A into local shared memory.\n"
"                for i in T.Parallel(N):\n"
"                    s_src[i] = A[i]\n"
"\n"
"                # Async-push s_src → s_dst in CTA 1, signal CTA 1's "
"barrier.\n"
"                T.copy_cluster(s_src, s_dst, dst_block=1,\n"
"                               remote_barrier=s_barrier[0])\n"
"\n"
"            if pid == 1:\n"
"                # Wait until CTA 0 finishes writing.\n"
"                T.mbarrier_wait_parity(s_barrier[0], 0)\n"
"\n"
"                for i in T.Parallel(N):\n"
"                    B[i] = s_dst[i]\n"
"\n"
"    return kernel\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:198
msgid "Generated producer code (single-thread guard, one PTX instruction):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:200
msgid ""
"if (((int)threadIdx.x) == 0) {\n"
"    tl::tma_store_cluster(&s_dst[0], &s_src[0], 1,\n"
"                          (uint32_t)(N * 4), s_barrier[0]);\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:207
msgid "Multi-TMA path — non-contiguous ND regions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:209
msgid ""
"When `remote_barrier` is provided but the copy region is not fully "
"contiguous (e.g. copying a 2-D slice `[0:M, 0:N_tile]` from a buffer of "
"shape `[M, N_full]` where `N_tile < N_full`), the compiler automatically "
"**decomposes the ND region into individual contiguous rows**, emitting one "
"`tl::tma_store_cluster` call per row. The mbarrier `arrive_count` is updated "
"to the total number of rows so the destination CTA's `mbarrier_wait_parity` "
"completes only after all rows are transferred."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:217
msgid ""
"# 2-D non-contiguous copy: N_tile < N_full → compiler emits M TMA calls\n"
"s_src = T.alloc_shared((M, N_full), \"float32\")\n"
"s_dst = T.alloc_shared((M, N_full), \"float32\")\n"
"s_barrier = T.alloc_cluster_barrier([1])   # arrive_count updated to M at "
"compile time\n"
"\n"
"T.copy_cluster(\n"
"    s_src[0:M, 0:N_tile],\n"
"    s_dst[0:M, 0:N_tile],\n"
"    dst_block=1,\n"
"    remote_barrier=s_barrier[0],\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:231
msgid ""
"The decomposition is recursive: a 3-D region `[0:D, 0:M, 0:N_tile]` (with "
"`N_tile < N_full`) produces `D × M` TMA calls and sets `arrive_count = D * "
"M`. Static extents are unrolled at compile time; symbolic extents emit TIR "
"`For` loops."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:236
msgid ""
"The API is identical to the fast path — no change is required in user code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:238
msgid "SIMT fallback — element-by-element stores"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:240
msgid "Omit `remote_barrier` to always use the SIMT fallback:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:242
msgid "T.copy_cluster(s_src, s_dst, dst_block=1)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:246
msgid ""
"This lowers to a SIMT parallel loop where every thread writes one (or a few) "
"elements into the remote CTA's shared memory via `cooperative_groups::"
"map_shared_rank`. Because `map_shared_rank` returns a scalar pointer, "
"vectorised writes are not possible. Use this path only when an mbarrier is "
"unavailable or when the tile is too small to justify barrier overhead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../programming_guides/cluster_tma.md:253
msgid ""
"When `remote_barrier` is provided but the region is neither contiguous nor "
"decomposable into TMA rows, the compiler falls back to SIMT stores and "
"**auto-injects a barrier arrive** (`__syncthreads()` + single-thread "
"`s_barrier.arrive(1u)`) so the destination CTA can still wait on the same "
"mbarrier without any API change."
msgstr ""

